{"name":"In for a Penny","hex":"#ee8877","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"in for a penny","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Ellipsis of in for a penny, in for a pound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in_for_a_penny"}],"entries":[{"title":"In for a Penny","blocks":[{"text":"\"In for a Penny\" is a song by English rock band Slade, released in 1975 as the lead single from their sixth studio album, Nobody's Fools. The song was written by lead vocalist Noddy Holder and bassist Jim Lea, and was produced by Chas Chandler. It reached number 11 in the UK Singles Chart and remained in the top 50 for eight weeks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/Sladesingle-inforapenny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_for_a_Penny","wikidata":"Q6009473"},{"title":"In for a Penny (game show)","blocks":[{"text":"In for a Penny is a British game show hosted by Stephen Mulhern, based on the segment of the same name in the show Ant & Dec's Saturday Night Takeaway. The show began airing on Saturday nights on ITV1 from 13 April 2019 to 8 June 2024."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7e/In_for_a_penny_logo.jpeg/330px-In_for_a_penny_logo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_for_a_Penny_(game_show)","wikidata":"Q65042398"},{"title":"For a Penny","blocks":[{"text":"\"For a Penny\" is a song by Pat Boone that reached number 23 on the Billboard Hot 100 in 1959."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/For_a_Penny","wikidata":"Q115958936"},{"title":"Penny","blocks":[{"text":"A penny is a coin or a unit of currency in various countries. Borrowed from the Carolingian denarius, it is usually the smallest denomination within a currency system. At present, it is the formal name of the British penny unit and the de facto name of the American one-cent coin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/1911-Australian-Penny-Reverse.jpg/330px-1911-Australian-Penny-Reverse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penny","wikidata":"Q234129"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Coin_of_Eric_Bloodaxe_Norse_king_of_York_952_954.jpg/330px-Coin_of_Eric_Bloodaxe_Norse_king_of_York_952_954.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Coin_of_Eric_Bloodaxe_Norse_king_of_York_952_954.jpg/330px-Coin_of_Eric_Bloodaxe_Norse_king_of_York_952_954.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoin_of_Eric_Bloodaxe_Norse_king_of_York_952_954.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Offa_king_of_Mercia_757_793_silver_penny.jpg/330px-Offa_king_of_Mercia_757_793_silver_penny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Offa_king_of_Mercia_757_793_silver_penny.jpg/330px-Offa_king_of_Mercia_757_793_silver_penny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOffa_king_of_Mercia_757_793_silver_penny.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/South_Africa-Penny-1929.jpg/330px-South_Africa-Penny-1929.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/South_Africa-Penny-1929.jpg/330px-South_Africa-Penny-1929.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouth_Africa-Penny-1929.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia